{
    "suite": "cose-sign",
    "description": "COSE cross-signing conformance (RFC 9052 / 9053 / 9338 / 9679). Every case is signed by both implementations and then handed to the other one to verify. Signing is deterministic (RFC 6979) on both sides, because that is the only mode in which two implementations can be compared byte for byte; the randomized mode is exercised by the cross-verification instead. The keys are the example keys of RFC 9052 and of the specification's worked example, and they secure nothing.",
